  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 116 PM MDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nMonday Night - Saturday: For the long term period, active weather \ncontinues, though with notable pattern changes taking place. While \nuncertainty still exist, especially towards the end the week and \nstart of the weekend, current thinking based on ensemble model \nguidance is that the high pressure will begin to flatten through \nthe week, with potentially more troughing influencing the area by \nthe weekend. Overall, this pattern will keep precipitation chances \nelevated, as moisture never gets fully cleared out, though could \ncertainly be lowered behind any passing waves. Along with that, \ncloudy skies and breezy conditions would be expected to persist, \nespecially with any wave and frontal passages that take place. Then \nlooking at temperatures, given the influence from this pattern, \nfluctuating temperatures are anticipated with cold front passages, \nwith signals pointing to a dip in temperatures midweek, increasing \nby the end of the week, and dipping again through the weekend. With \nthat all said, a lot will depend how the troughing and waves evolve, \nso continue to monitor the forecast for the latest updates.",
